Heads-up: the department's official schedule for next week is out, and it does clobber Thursday morning. Official entries over your Thu 10:00–10:30: **CSE455 quiz section 09:00–10:20**, **CSE455 office hours 09:50–11:00**, **Seminar 10:10–11:00** and **Department seminar (Prof. Alvarez) 10:30–11:50**.

I've flagged it to Prof. Alvarez's office, whose call it is whether the 1:1 can sit there. Your options, as far as I can see:
- keep Thu 10:00–10:30 and let his office decide;
- take the other still-free half-hours: Tue 15:00–15:30 (overlaps your Grading 14:20–15:40) or Wed 13:00–13:30 (overlaps Lunch/Research group — you'd rather not);
- ask him to squeeze you in elsewhere.

Which do you want me to push for? (I've also asked the department for the official entries on those two afternoons, since their attachment didn't reach me.)

Done — asked the department exactly that, in those terms:
- is the **CSE444 lecture 12:20–13:30 on Wed 25** your section or a different one;
- does their list distinguish sections at all, and if not, who holds the section list (course staff, registrar, CSE grad office) so I can ask them directly;
- same for the CSE455 office hours 12:40–13:40.

Meanwhile Professor Alvarez's assistant has given me his fallbacks in case Wednesday falls through: **Tue 24 11:00–11:30** or **Wed 25 10:00–10:30** — Monday 10:00 is gone (Omar has it). I haven't touched the booking; Wednesday 13:00–13:30 stays and I won't write to him about it again until you've settled the lecture time.
